1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,987
In the beginning, the old stories say, there was only dark water, and on it, a golden egg.

2
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:10,086
Hiranyagarbha. The golden womb.

3
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:19,907
When it broke, one half became the sky, and the other, the earth. And the one who woke inside was Brahma, the creator.

4
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:29,239
He has four faces, so that he sees in every direction at once. From each of his four mouths came one of the four Vedas.

5
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:43,370
From his mind, he brought forth sons. Among them were the seven great sages, the Saptarishi.

6
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:49,050
Their light still turns above us, in the seven stars of the Great Bear.

7
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:57,050
In his four hands, he holds what a world needs to begin.

8
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:59,859
A water pot, for the waters of life.

9
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:08,240
A string of beads, to count out time.

10
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:15,919
The sacred Vedas, for knowledge.

11
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:24,859
And a lotus, for all that grows pure from the mud.

12
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:36,022
His mount is the swan, which is said to separate milk from water: the gift of telling the true from the false.

13
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:41,911
Saraswati, goddess of knowledge and music, rides the same white swan.

14
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:51,218
One flower carries his name. High in the Himalaya, the Brahma kamal opens at night, in the brief summer of the mountains.

15
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:57,995
It grows between 3,000 and 4,800 metres, where little else can bloom.

16
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:07,194
One day of Brahma lasts 4,320,000,000 years, and his night is just as long.

17
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:11,779
He lives for a hundred such years. And then the universe rests.

18
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:22,702
Few temples are built for him. The best known stands at Pushkar, in Rajasthan, beside a lake said to have formed where his lotus fell.

19
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:30,440
Pilgrims come to bathe at its 52 ghats, most of all at the full moon of Kartik, in the autumn.

20
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:39,874
And the hour before dawn still carries his name: Brahma muhurta, the creator's hour, when the world is about to begin again.

21
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:48,214
It begins about an hour and a half before sunrise: a time kept for quiet, for study, and for prayer.
